-- title:
--   Theorem 8.1 — an asymptotic coupling forces equality of stationary distributions
-- statement:
--   Let $\{\mathcal P_t\}=\{\mathcal P_t,t\ge 0\}$ be a Markov transition semigroup on a separable metric space $\mathbf X$ admitting two stationary distributions $\mu_1$ and $\mu_2$. For $i=1,2$ let $P_{\mu_i}$ denote the distribution of the Markov process with initial distribution $\mu_i$ and transition semigroup $\{\mathcal P_t\}$ on $(\mathbb D(\mathbf X),\mathcal B(\mathbb D(\mathbf X)))$. Suppose there is an asymptotic coupling of $P_{\mu_1}$ and $P_{\mu_2}$. Then $\mu_1=\mu_2$.
--
--   The joint process is a $2J$-dimensional process driven by a $J$-dimensional Brownian motion, so standard irreducibility arguments are unavailable. This abstract criterion replaces them, and it needs no completeness of the state space, which matters because $\mathbb X$ is not Polish.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: B(D(X)) for the Skorokhod J₁ topology → the σ-algebra generated by the coordinate maps; reason: the two agree for a separable metric space
--   - encoding: the distribution of the Markov process on D(X) → a probability measure m on Cadlag S with initial law μ and the Markov property in integrated form (IsMarkovLaw); reason: this characterizes the distribution; the theorem speaks of laws that exist as RCLL laws
-- source:
--   Lipshutz, Ramanan, Sensitivity analysis for the stationary distribution of RBM, arXiv:1907.00472v2, https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.00472v2, Theorem 8.1, p.33 (cited: continuous version of [16, Theorem 1.1])

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_RBMSensitivity_IsMarkovSemigroup
import Definitions.Def_RBMSensitivity_IsStationaryLaw
import Definitions.Def_RBMSensitivity_IsMarkovLaw
import Definitions.Def_RBMSensitivity_IsAsymptoticCoupling
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Filter Topology
open scoped NNReal ENNReal RealInnerProductSpace

namespace RBMSensitivity

/-- **Theorem 8.1** (continuous version of [16, Theorem 1.1]): arXiv:1907.00472v2, p.33. Let `{P_t}` be a
Markov transition semigroup on a separable metric space `S` admitting two stationary distributions `μ₁` and
`μ₂`. For `i = 1, 2` let `P_{μ_i}` denote the distribution of the Markov process with initial distribution
`μ_i` and transition semigroup `{P_t}` on `D(S)`. Suppose there is an asymptotic coupling of `P_{μ₁}` and
`P_{μ₂}`. Then `μ₁ = μ₂`.

**Formalization Note.** Completeness of `S` is deliberately not assumed: the paper relaxes it, and it fails
for `X` (Remark 3.1). `m₁, m₂` are the laws `P_{μ_i}`. -/
theorem theorem_8_1 {S : Type*} [MetricSpace S] [TopologicalSpace.SeparableSpace S]
    [MeasurableSpace S] [BorelSpace S] {Pt : ℝ≥0 → Kernel S S} (hP : IsMarkovSemigroup Pt)
    {μ₁ μ₂ : Measure S} (hμ₁ : IsStationaryLaw Pt μ₁) (hμ₂ : IsStationaryLaw Pt μ₂)
    {m₁ m₂ : Measure (Cadlag S)} (hm₁ : IsMarkovLaw Pt μ₁ m₁) (hm₂ : IsMarkovLaw Pt μ₂ m₂)
    {Υ : Measure (Cadlag S × Cadlag S)} (hΥ : IsAsymptoticCoupling m₁ m₂ Υ) :
    μ₁ = μ₂ := by sorry

end RBMSensitivity
